    {"number":49,"title":"tools: expand li.s as SN's assembler does; PAL C for 27 functions it unblocks","author":"chistianh","draft":false,"head":"pal-oficial-10","events":["merged"],"mergedBy":"Veradictus","additions":878,"deletions":8,"changedFiles":33,"body":"Title: tools: expand li.s as SN's assembler does; PAL C for 27 functions it unblocks\nThe tool change\nGCC writes every float constant as li.s $fN, value. Retail's assembler, SN's ps2eeas, always builds the value in $at: lui, plus ori when the low half is not zero, then mtc1. The driver's GNU as does that only when the low half is zero. For any other value, at -G8, it puts the value in .lit4 and loads it with one lwc1 ...($gp). That is one word instead of three, plus a $gp access retail does not…"},
